[style name="Interaction_Style"]
if {Dead_person_choice} == 1:
	join Town_Leader rightmost
	join Thorinn (normal) leftmost
	Town_Leader: Thorinn, you've saved them! Truly, you are a gift to Rockfall!
	Thorinn: Lets not forget the one who paid the ultimate price.
	Town_Leader: The lives of others in not to be played with. I do understand however that dire circumstances call for desperate measures.
	Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
	Malrik: What will you do now doctor...?
	- Publicly credit Malric
		set {Blame_choice} = 2
		Thorinn: This cure wasn't mine alone. Malric's knowledge made this possible.
		Town_Leader: Malric? That explains... I'd hoped never to hear that name again.
		Town_Leader: But if what you say is the truth, then even in the darkest of souls you can find a spark of light.
		Town_Leader: Do be careful, even thogh he was of great help this time, following his ways will lead to a dangerous path we do not condone.
		leave Town_Leader
		Thorinn: *Turning to Malric in the shadows*
		join Malrik rightmost
		Malrik: A rare day, doctor. They don't hate me quite as much... for now. You have my thanks.
	- Accept the credit
		set {Blame_choice} = 1
		Thorinn (normal): I just did what had to be done.
		Thorinn: Vivian was the purest soul that managed to save everyone. Lets honour her by never forgetting her kindness.
	- Thank Malric in private
		set {Blame_choice} = 3
		Thorinn: I just did what had to be done.
		leave Town_Leader
		join Malrik rightmost
		Thorinn: *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
		Thorinn: I know I didn't mention you, but know this, you have my thanks.
		Thorinn: Without your help I wouldn't have been able to create the antidote.
		Malrik: So that's how it is. I had hoped for a glimpse of salvation in return. Secrets weigh heavy doctor.

elif {Dead_person_choice} == 2:
	join Town_Leader rightmost
	join Thorinn (agitated) leftmost
	Town_Leader: Thorinn, you tried your best, but this time it was not enough.
	Town_Leader: Only one saved and so many lost. Couldn't you have done more?
	Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
	Malrik: What will you do now doctor...?
	- Admit fault
		set {Blame_choice} = 1
		Thorinn (agitated): I really did the best I could.
		Town_Leader: Your capabilities as a doctor have proven to be less than what you've promised.
	- Publicly blame Malric
		set {Blame_choice} = 2
		Thorinn: This failure wasn't mine alone. Malric's evil ways made this possible.
		Town_Leader: Malric? That explains... I'd hoped never to hear that name again.
		Thorinn: He led me astray with his twisted words!
		leave Town_Leader
		join Malrik rightmost
		Malrik: ...!
		Malrik: You've got no idea whose name you've just tarnished.
	- Confront Malric in private
		set {Blame_choice} = 3
		Thorinn (agitated): I really did the best I could.
		Town_Leader: Your capabilities as a doctor have proven to be less than what you've promised.
		leave Town_Leader
		Thorinn (agitated): *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
		join Malrik rightmost
		Thorinn: I didn't expose you, but know this, you also had a hand in this failure and I'll never forgive you for it.
		Malrik: I've warned you sufficiently but you did not want to listen because your judgement was clouded by the rumours fed to you by the village.

elif {Dead_person_choice} == 3:
	join Town_Leader rightmost
	join Thorinn (agitated) leftmost
	Town_Leader: Thorinn, you tried your best but you only half succeeded.
	Town_Leader: You killed one of us to save three, and yet, two more are dead. Was it worth the life of an innocent?
	Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
	Malrik: What will you do now doctor...?
	- Accept the responsibility
		set {Blame_choice} = 1
		Thorinn: I did what was in my power.
		Town_Leader: We might disagree if this was the right choice, but Astrid's sacrifice saved three lives.
		Town_Leader: Let's forever honour her memory.
	- Publicly put the responsibility on Malric
		set {Blame_choice} = 2
		Thorinn: This cure wasn't mine alone. Malric's knowledge made this possible.
		Town_Leader: Malric? That explains... I'd hoped never to hear that name again.
		Thorinn: I'm not guilt free, but if Malric didn't trick me, this could've been avoided.
		Thorinn: I will make sure not to trust Malric's misleading words from now on.
		leave Town_Leader
		join Malrik rightmost
		Malrik: ...!
		Malrik: You've got no idea whose name you've just tarnished.
	- Confront Malric in private
		set {Blame_choice} = 3
		Thorinn: I did what was in my power.
		leave Town_Leader
		Thorinn: *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
		join Malrik rightmost
		Thorinn: I didn't mention you, but know this, you had a hand in this aswell.
		Thorinn: Your cryptic messages caused this loss.
		Malrik: I've warned you sufficiently.
		Malrik: It isn't my fault that you didn't trust my word enough, as your judgement was clouded by the rumours fed to you by the village.

elif {Dead_person_choice} == 4:
	join Town_Leader rightmost
	join Thorinn (agitated) leftmost
	Town_Leader: Thorinn, you came with hope and promises, but we are left with grief. Five lives were lost under your care. You had a strong opinion doctor but you should've consulted us.
	Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
	Malrik: Seems like your good intentions weren't of much help this time. What will you tell them now?
	- Admit fault
		set {Blame_choice} = 1
		Thorinn (agitated): I tried to find a way that wouldn’t cause more harm than what was already done, but in the end, I failed them. I will always carry this burden.
		Town_Leader: You speak of burdens, but what about the mourning families? You had a choice, doctor, and you chose wrong.
	
	- Publicly blame Malric
		set {Blame_choice} = 2
		Thorinn (agitated): I admit that I did know of a cure, but it was based on Malric's twisted words.
		Thorinn: I had a choice to make, a terrible choice, take an innocent life or let these people die. I just couldn't cross that line.
		Thorinn: Malric is too far gone in his ways of dark magic, there wasn't even a guarantee this was going to work.
		Town_Leader: I understand you didn't want to give into Malric's dishonourable ways.
		leave Town_Leader
		join Malrik rightmost
		Malrik: ...!
		Malrik: You've got no idea whose name you've just tarnished.
if {Dead_person_choice} != 0:
	leave --All--
	[signal arg="start_night"]
	[wait time="2.0"]
	jump Final_summary/
